<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! Contract

`[memes[]]` emits every title in the wiki that reads as a `lar:` URI, delegating the recognition to `allLarTitles`. It acts as a ''collection source'': it disregards the input pipeline entirely, so it opens a run rather than narrowing one.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/name-law>>

!! The Registered Name

TW5 binds a filter operator to its ''exported binding'', never to a file path and never to a doc-comment. The export reads `memes`, so the operator answers to `memes[]`; renaming the export renames the operator and silently unbinds every filter run that spelled the old name.

The module header inside the source carries the registration triple TW5 reads at boot — `title` (the `lar:` address), `type: application/javascript`, `module-type: filteroperator`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/source>>

